<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7611" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνατέλλω</span></b> , poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντ-</span></b> , aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέτειλα</span>: pf.
		part.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνατεταλκός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					9.15.10
				</span></i>
			:—<i>make to rise up,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖσιν δ᾽</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵπποις</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ἀμβροσίην ἀνέτειλενέμεσθυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.777
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἴγυπτος . . Δήμητρος ἀντέλλει
					στάχυν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					300
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				3.18
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ ἀ.</span>
			<i>make</i> water <i>gush forth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				6(5).75
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἥλιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
					5.45
				</span></i>
			:—so in 
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλὸξ ἀνατελλομένα</span> a
			flame <i>mounting up,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ion</u>
				4(3).83
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bring forth, give birth to</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄντειλας Διόνυσον</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				7(6).5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰούλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.44
				</span></i>
			: of events, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυρί᾽ ἀπ᾽
				α&lt;&gt;σχρῶν ἀνατέλλοντα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1139
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>rise, appear above the horizon,</i> of any heavenly body,
			as sun and moon, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.142
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1246
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				754
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ἠῶ τε καὶ ἥλιον ἀνατέλλοντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.204
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				4.40
			</span></i>; also of constellations, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.959
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠὼσἀντ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.1007
				</span></i>
			; dist. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτέλλω</span>
			(q.v.), <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Alm.</u>
				8.4
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνατολή.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτέλλω</span>
			, of the Pleiades, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				13.25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of a river,
				<i>take its rise,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ ταύτης [γῆς λίμνης</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.52
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				14.16
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> of
			persons, <i>originate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ Ἰούδα ἀνατέταλκεν ὁ κύριος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Heb.</u>
					7.14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>grow,</i> of hair, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταρφὺς ἀντέλλουσα θρίξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					535
				</span></i>
			; of teeth, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				501b29
			</span></i>; <i>spring up,</i> of plants, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.1.6
			</span></i>, al.; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνατολή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> of mountains,
				<i>rise,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.501
			</span></i>; but, <i>appear on the horizon,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				601
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>rise up,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέτειλε σωτήρ</span> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				978
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Philae</span>).</div>
